-- An entity of TWO extra classes at once (#1143). Its classes are the list in its `parents` property (`cls:<name>` ids, the ISA kinds): the getters of both apply, the setter of each fires (a kind's
-- setter needs its ISA parent entity `cls:<name>`), and the list survives a journal replay. A `parents` write on an entity that already exists binds the getters of its kinds (they are bound at birth
-- otherwise). Converted from tests/multi_class_1143.rs.

test a parents write on an existing entity binds the getters and setters of both kinds
PACK two 1
Alpha.sa getter: 'alpha:' + str(this.n)
Beta.sb getter: 'beta:' + str(this.n)
Alpha.go_a on-setter run-a:
  WHEN this.go_a == True:
    this.did_a = True
Beta.go_b on-setter run-b:
  WHEN this.go_b == True:
    this.did_b = True
-- the ISA parent entities a kind's setter needs
given cls:alpha {"name": "Alpha"}
given cls:beta {"name": "Beta"}
given Thing:x {"n": 3}
-- no kind yet: no getter
reads Thing:x.sa = null
write Thing:x.parents = ["cls:alpha", "cls:beta"]
-- both getters apply
reads Thing:x.sa = "alpha:3"
reads Thing:x.sb = "beta:3"
write Thing:x.n = 4
-- both follow a write
reads Thing:x.sa = "alpha:4"
reads Thing:x.sb = "beta:4"
write Thing:x.go_a = true
write Thing:x.go_b = true
-- both setters fire
reads Thing:x.did_a = true
reads Thing:x.did_b = true

-- The root class `Entity` is implicit (#1143): a getter on it applies to every entity, and a getter of the entity's own class beats it.
test a getter on entity applies to every entity and a nearer class beats it
load root.c1f
load own_layer.c1f
given Thing:x {"n": 1}
given Own:z {}
-- the implicit root class
reads Thing:x.summary = "Thing Thing:x"
reads Own:z.summary = "own"

test the class list survives a journal replay
PACK two 1
Alpha.sa getter: 'alpha:' + str(this.n)
Beta.sb getter: 'beta:' + str(this.n)
Alpha.go_a on-setter run-a:
  WHEN this.go_a == True:
    this.did_a = True
Beta.go_b on-setter run-b:
  WHEN this.go_b == True:
    this.did_b = True
given cls:alpha {"name": "Alpha"}
given cls:beta {"name": "Beta"}
given Thing:x {"n": 3}
write Thing:x.parents = ["cls:alpha", "cls:beta"]
write Thing:x.n = 4
write Thing:x.go_a = true
write Thing:x.go_b = true
-- a journal replay into a fresh engine gives the same entity
replay
same Thing:x
reads Thing:x.sa = "alpha:4"
reads Thing:x.did_b = true
